# MSc AI Capstone Project - Core Structure

## Project Context
MSc Artificial Intelligence capstone project focused on developing domain-specific AI for educational syllabus generation.

### Core Problem
Current LLMs can generate text that looks like a syllabus but lack specific educational structure and pedagogical understanding for coherent, educationally sound course content.

### Solution Approach
Building a domain-specific AI model that:
- Takes minimal inputs (course description, learning objectives, problem statements)
- Generates structured, coherent course syllabi
- Understands educational frameworks and learning progression
- Maintains pedagogical quality throughout content

### Technical Innovation
- Custom neural architecture for educational content structure
- Specialized word embeddings trained on educational terminology
- Sequence-to-sequence modeling with attention mechanisms
- Training data from Open Syllabus Project API and educational resources

## Directory Organization
- `@docs/` - Academic documentation, literature review, methodology, progress reports
- `@research/` - Literature collection, analysis, datasets research  
- `@src/` - Source code (data processing, models, training, evaluation, utilities)
- `@experiments/` - Experimental code, baseline models, custom architectures
- `@data/` - Raw, processed, and synthetic datasets
- `@notebooks/` - Jupyter notebooks for exploration and prototyping
- `@Notes/` - Course notes and existing project documents

## File Naming Conventions
- Python files: snake_case
- Classes: PascalCase
- Functions/variables: snake_case
- Constants: UPPER_CASE
- Notebooks: descriptive names with dates for experiments
- Academic docs: structured with proper versioning

